      "value": "I will ask the same questions as last time.\n\nCan you be more specific here? Why are you using IKFollower in this case, since it doesn't appear to be an emitter that requires worldspace emission?\n\nIs it parented directly to your head bone? It looks like it is parented to the ear bone, which is not an IK-driven bone.\n\nIt seems like the effect you desire is simply a world-space particle being emitted as a child of a non-IK'd bone. You may be able to get this to work without IKFollower, but if not, then you will be unable to use the particle in this case. This is not the intended use of IKFollower.\n\nPlease test a case with a simple emitter paired from one of the compatible bones listed in our documentation, firing a particle into worldspace.\n\nhttps://docs.vrchat.com/v2019.1.1/docs/vrc_ikfollower",
      "viewerReactions": null
    },
